;; Written by Claude, 2026-10-14, for Phase 17 (design section 20,
;; proposal 9, approved by the user); reviewed by the user, 2026-10-14. It
;; replaces the file the user reviewed on 2026-10-14. Why this is right:
;; - Card and CardHex are new (proposal 9), as on LLVM: each copies its
;;   two HUGEINT parameters, passed by reference, to its frame (MOVQ
;;   @4(AP), @8(AP)) and calls FORMATTEDOUTPUT_CARD or _CARDHE with
;;   stream LineOutput.output (CLRL) and the addresses of quadword
;;   copies. The two .EXTERNALs are new; FormattedOutput's key, which it
;;   imports, and Out's own (.IDENT, POC_K1_) are new. The header
;;   comment is one line longer and the procedures come before Flush, so
;;   every line number after them is 16 more, the one a trap passes
;;   (PUSHL) included.
;; The rest is as the user reviewed it on 2026-10-14:
;; - Flush now calls POC_FLUSH_OUTPUT (.EXTERNAL, CALLS #0), PocRtl's
;;   routine that writes Out's line so far to a terminal without ending
;;   it, and does nothing to a file. The header comment is six lines
;;   longer, so every line number after it is six more, the one a trap
;;   passes (PUSHL #88) included.
;; The rest is as the user reviewed it on 2026-10-13:
;; - Out now imports FormattedOutput, not FormattedText, and calls it
;;   for everything but IsConsole, as on LLVM; its own Field is gone. Its
;;   initializer calls LINEOUTPUT_INIT, then FORMATTEDOUTPUT_INIT, then
;;   FindConsole.
;; - Each of Char, String, Ln, Int, Hex, Real and LongReal passes its
;;   stream, LineOutput.output (CLRL), as the first argument, then its own
;;   parameters as before: CHAR and INTEGER as longwords, the open array
;;   as address and length, a HUGEINT as the address of a quadword copy,
;;   a REAL by value (MOVF), a LONGREAL as the address of a copy (MOVG).
;; - Ten passes e as a longword to FORMATTEDOUTPUT_TEN and returns its
;;   G_floating result in R0 and R1; a function that reached its END
;;   would trap (12).
;; - IsConsole is an exported BOOLEAN ("::"). FindConsole copies
;;   "SYS$OUTPUT" (MOVC5, 10 bytes, zero-filled to 16) and calls
;;   POC_IS_TERMINAL, Platform's routine ($GETDVIW, DVI$_DEVCLASS
;;   DC$_TERM), with its address and length 10, and sets IsConsole when
;;   R0 is 1. Unchanged.
;; - Out's key is new: its interface is the same, but its symbol file
;;   lists its imports, now FormattedOutput and LineOutput.
;; - On the guest every fixture that prints through Out prints what it
;;   printed before.
;; Compiled here in a program that contains Modules (section 19.5): it
;; differs from vax-out/expected-vax-Out.mar only by the descriptor, the
;; .EXTERNAL POC_MODULE, the block "its descriptor, for Modules" and the
;; initializer's PUSHAL L_MODULE_DESCRIPTOR and CALLS #1, G^POC_MODULE.
; Out, written by poc (doc/developer/vax-macro32-backend.md)
